    "html": "<p>Monochromatic light is incident on a metal surface and photoelectrons are emitted from the surface. The maximum kinetic energy of the emitted electrons is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.50\"></span> eV and the work function of the metal is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0\"></span> eV. What is the best estimate for the wavelength of the incident light?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"400\"></span> nm</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"500\"></span> nm</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"600\"></span> nm</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"700\"></span> nm</li>\n</ol>"
  },
